  best magnitude anywhere on the frontier: 0.236 dB
  best phase     anywhere on the frontier: 2.8 deg

  ⭐ READ THIS AS THE RESULT. Minimum phase is the MAXIMUM-LEAD realisation of
  a given magnitude (any other causal realisation is min-phase x an all-pass,
  and an all-pass only ADDS lag). So if the measured phase cannot be reached by
  a min-phase cascade that also matches the magnitude, NO causal linear element
  of ANY order can supply this target -- which is a stronger statement than
  session 50's reachability result (that ruled out the elements the model
  contains; this rules out the whole CLASS).

=== 2d. CAN THE PHASE MEASUREMENT'S KNOWN BIAS EXPLAIN THE SHORTFALL? ===
  The blend-axis quadratic gives Q = Re(g1) EXACTLY but r = sqrt(|g1|^2 + H)
  with H the band's harmonic power, so cos(theta) = Q/r is biased TOWARDS 90 deg
  and r is an UPPER BOUND on the fundamental. Correcting it moves theta away
  from 90 deg, which REDUCES the required lead over 127-640 Hz -- so it is a
  live explanation. Sizing it as the implied harmonic-to-fundamental power:
       f    th_ped th needed     d deg  implied H/P
      40     139.0     111.8     -27.3   impossible
      50     143.5      96.4     -47.2   impossible
      64     132.6      82.6     -50.0    sign flip
      80     114.1      73.1     -41.0    sign flip
     101      93.2      63.7     -29.4    sign flip
     127      72.9      52.3     -20.6          3.3
     160      53.9      37.9     -16.0          0.8
     202      40.0      23.0     -17.0          0.4
     254      53.8      13.5     -40.3          1.7
     403      78.1      23.4     -54.7         18.8
     508      70.1      33.2     -36.9          5.0
     640      83.3      38.0     -45.3         44.5
     806      97.8      55.7     -42.1    sign flip
    1016      94.2      58.5     -35.6    sign flip
    1613      57.2      44.9     -12.3          0.7

  'implied H/P' is the harmonic-to-fundamental POWER ratio the bias would need
  in order to reconcile the measurement with the min-phase fit. H/P = 0.1 is
  ~32%% THD; H/P = 1 is more harmonic power than fundamental. 'impossible' means
  the bias would have to act in the WRONG DIRECTION (deflate r), which harmonic
  power cannot do; 'sign flip' means no inflation of any size suffices.

  DELAY CHECK: best-fit pure delay -0.101 ms leaves 29.7 deg rms; a FLAT offset
  of -34.4 deg leaves 12.8 deg rms. Shortfall span -54.7 to -12.3 deg over a 40x
  frequency range => FLAT, not proportional to f: a delay-compensation mismatch on the OD path is
     EXCLUDED as the cause.
  => the bias CANNOT explain the shortfall at the bands that carry it.

